mary><p class="faq-answer">Not for most people. Dyson upright vacuums can be powerful, but they are often heavy, expensive, and not clearly better ownership value than Shark’s strongest upright options.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>What makes upright vacuums fail over time?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Common failure points include clogged filters, hair-wrapped brushrolls, cracked hoses, weak latches, worn belts, and airflow loss from poor maintenance.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Who should not buy an upright vacuum?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Avoid a full-size upright if your top priorities are very light weight, quick daily pickups, small-space storage, or cleaning lots of stairs. A cordless vacuum may fit those situations better.</p></details>
